  "solution": {
    "text": "Find the volume by either<br /><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> or <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> and match it with the values given in graph to find correct.<br /><br />Volume of 1 mole of an ideal gas at 273 K and 1 atm is 22.4 L and that at 373 K and 1 atm pressure is calculated as<br /><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.082</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>373</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>30.58</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>≃</mo><mn>30.6</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math>",
